A||||4||JohnnyK||Running rich AND lean??||||4||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||03-23-2000||06:13 PM||||Ok, my Fiero goes, but spits fluid out of the exhaust (looks like oil and water, but doesn't look like it's burning the oil?) so I ran the diagnostic thing and it said code 45 (Running rich, replace o2 sensor).. Fine, done. It ran good for about 1 minute, then crap started shooting out, and now it gives me a code 44 (running lean, replace o2).. what gives? Thanks<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||theogre||03-23-2000||07:24 PM||||water all the time or just when cold? just when cold could be water and soot. water when hot and you've got a blown head or intake.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||03-23-2000||10:10 PM||||After engine is warmed up and any condensation in exhaust system is evaporated out:<P>Check your oil for water, and your water for oil.<P>Bubbles in your coolant when running? May not be easy to check in Fieros.  Oil discolored? Kind of foamy or whitish?  All are signs of blown head gasket.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||03-23-2000||11:34 PM||||I never got to the point where the engine was warm.. I was kinda upset that the engine light came on after changing the o2 sensor... Is this common?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||03-24-2000||07:01 PM||||a. did you reset the ECM?<BR>b. If you did you have to drive it some. Then once it worms up shut it off, reset it again, then drive it at least 30-45 minutes around town and maybe a short highway run.<P>Then if you still get the error you either got a bad O2 or you have some other problem.||||reg||1
